(PRC-87 — undocumented precision: every path-taking statement in this
 section accepts an empty path and fails cleanly through the error flag.
 Not a manual claim — the manual says nothing about degenerate paths — but
 it is the memory-safety floor for the whole section and the first thing a
 leaf will emit by accident, so it is on the record.
 `Create a device node` is absent from the list because an empty TYPE is
 rejected at compile time, not at run time; see D2.vox.
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-87.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   an empty path to create errored
   an empty path to remove errored
   an empty path to change directory errored
   an empty path to symbolic link errored
   an empty path to mount errored
   an empty path to unmount errored
   an empty path to pivot root errored
   an empty path to execute errored
   nothing crashed
)
